    "https://jobs.ucf.edu/jobs/information-security-professional-ii-orlando-florida-united-states-6f812c39-358b-447b-88fb-28597cfaa771": {
      "title": "Information Security Professional II",
      "description": "Information Security Professional II - Orlando, Florida, United States University of Central Florida Navigation Home Meet Our People Featured Jobs Resources Faculty Join Our Talent Network Search Jobs Kiosk mode Information Security Professional II Information Technology (A&P) Skip to section BENEFITS WHY UCF? ABOUT ORLANDO My Profile Ready to Apply? Information Security Professional II R114453 Main Campus, Orlando, Florida Staff Full time Closing at: Oct 23 2026 - 12:00am EDT ISO- Identity & Access Mgmt University Operations: The University Operations division at UCF is committed to creating a supportive and welcoming environment for our faculty, staff, students, and the broader community. We take pride in delivering exceptional service, sharing our expertise, and upholding the highest standards to ensure a world-class campus experience. Visit our website or follow us on Facebook and Instagram to learn more. The Opportunity: University Operations is seeking to hire an Information Security Professional II. This role supports the university’s Identity Governance and Access Management (IGAM) program by administering, monitoring, and improving identity lifecycle and access management processes for enterprise systems and institutional users This position performs operational and technical work related to identity provisioning, access governance, role-based access control, privileged access processes, compliance activities, reporting, documentation, and stakeholder support. The role works closely with campus partners to help ensure appropriate access to university resources while maintaining security, compliance, and data integrity. Responsibilities: Identity Lifecycle Management Manage identity lifecycle activities for students, faculty, staff, researchers, guests, affiliates, and sponsored accounts. Perform account provisioning, de-provisioning, modifications, affiliation updates, and reconciliation activities across institutional systems. Ensure identity processes are completed accurately and in accordance with university policies and standards. Access Management & Authorization Support Review, process, and support access requests for enterprise applications and services. Apply established access models, business rules, and authorization procedures to ensure appropriate access based on role and business need. Assist users and business units with access-related questions and requests. Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) Maintain role-based access control structures, entitlement mappings, and access assignment processes. Support updates, testing, and documentation of access models and authorization frameworks. Partner with business and technical teams to resolve access-related issues. Access Reviews, Audits & Compliance Support periodic access reviews, audit requests, and compliance assessments. Collect and validate access records, identify potential access discrepancies, and track remediation efforts. Maintain documentation and evidence required for compliance and audit activities. Privileged Access Governance Support governance processes for privileged accounts, administrative access, service accounts, application registrations, and other high-risk identities. Maintain inventories, assist with reviews, and support exception tracking activities. Help ensure privileged access processes remain documented, controlled, and auditable. Stakeholder Support & Collaboration Provide support to university stakeholders, application owners, distributed IT teams, and information security partners. Troubleshoot identity and access issues within the scope of the role and escalate complex governance or risk-related matters as appropriate. Serve as backup support for other Identity Governance and Access Management team functions. Documentation & Process Improvement Develop and maintain standard operating procedures, work instructions, and knowledge base articles. Identify opportunities to improve efficiency, strengthen controls, reduce manual effort, and enhance the user experience. Support continuous improvement initiatives within the Identity Governance and Access Management program. Reporting & Data Analysis Prepare and maintain identity and access management reports using approved tools and data sources. Perform data quality reviews, reconciliation activities, and access trend analysis. Protect sensitive identity, access, and security information while supporting management reporting needs. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 2 years of relevant experience; or High School Diploma (or equivalent) and 6 years of relevant work experience in lieu of degree; or an equivalent combination of education and experience pursuant to Fla. Stat. 112.219(6) . Preferred Qualifications : Experience with Identity Governance and Administration (IGA) or Identity and Access Management (IAM) platforms. Knowledge of identity lifecycle management, provisioning, and de-provisioning processes. Experience supporting role-based access control (RBAC) and access governance practices. Familiarity with privileged access management concepts and controls. Experience supporting audits, compliance reviews, and access certifications. Strong analytical, problem-solving, and documentation skills. Ability to communicate effectively with technical and non-technical stakeholders. Experience working in higher education or other complex enterprise environments. Special Instructions to the Applicants: Position requires a valid Class E driver’s license. This position may involve driving to various locations on and off campus to conduct University business. The anticipated salary range for this position is $64,518 - $80,000. The final salary will be determined based on the candidate's qualifications, experience, and internal equity considerations. All applicants must be authorized to work for any U.S. employer. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position, and the university cannot accommodate H‑1B transfers or employment-based visa processing for individuals currently sponsored by another employer. This role requires the successful candidate to work on-site at UCF as their primary work location. On-site presence is an essential function of this role. UCF is seeking to fill multiple roles. Candidates for this job posting will be considered for additional Information Security Professional II vacancies in this department. Are you ready to unleash YOUR potential? As a next-generation public research university and Forbes-ranked top employer in Florida, we are a community of thinkers, doers, creators, innovators, healers, and leaders striving to create broader prosperity and help shape a better future. No matter what your role is, when you join Knight Nation, you’ll play an integral role at one of the most impactful universities in the country. You’ll be met with opportunities to connect and collaborate with talented faculty, staff, and students across 12 colleges and multiple campuses, engaging in impactful work that makes a positive difference. Your time at UCF will provide you with many meaningful opportunities to grow, you’ll work alongside talented colleagues on complex projects that will challenge you and help you gain new skills, and you’ll have countless rewarding experiences that go well beyond a paycheck. Working at UCF has its perks! UCF offers: Benefit packages, including Medical, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending, and Employee Assistance Program Paid time off, including annual and sick time off and paid holidays Retirement savings options Employee discounts, including tickets to many Orlando attractions Education assistance And more…For more benefits information, view the UCF Employee Benefits Guide . Dive into our Total Rewards Calculator to discover the diverse selection available to you, giving you a glimpse into the benefits that together shape your comprehensive rewards package at UCF. Unless explicitly stated on the job posting, it is UCF’s expectation that an employee of UCF will reside in Florida as of the date the employment begins. Department UCF IT Information Security Office Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:00am - 5:00pm Type of Appointment Regular Expected Salary $64,518.00 to Negotiable Job Posting End Date 10-23-2026-12-00-AM The University of Central Florida is an equal opportunity employer that does not discriminate against any employee or applicant for employment based on any characteristic protected by law.  The University maintains programs for protected veterans and individuals with disabilities in accordance with all applicable federal and state laws. As a Florida public university, the University of Central Florida makes all application materials and selection procedures available to the public upon request. UCF is proud to be a smoke-free campus and an E-Verify employer. For general application or posting questions, please email talent@ucf.edu . If an accommodation due to a disability is needed to apply for this position, please email onac@ucf.edu . People Also Viewed Plumber I Orlando Facilities (USPS) Data Engineer IV, Data Platforms Orlando Information Technology (A&P) Constituent Services Coordinator Orlando Administrative Management and (A&P) Want to be notified when we post new jobs?  Sign up here! First Name (required) 4be8f2ef Last Name (required) 6f152a76 Email (required) 8825cd52 Phone Number 159164c0 244 results found No results found Afghanistan (+93) Åland Islands (+358) Albania (+355) Algeria (+213) American Samoa (+1) Andorra (+376) Angola (+244) Anguilla (+1) Antigua & Barbuda (+1) Argentina (+54) Armenia (+374) Aruba (+297) Ascension Island (+247) Australia (+61) Austria (+43) Azerbaijan (+994) Bahamas (+1) Bahrain (+973) Bangladesh (+880) Barbados (+1) Belarus (+375) Belgium (+32) Belize (+501) Benin (+229) Bermuda (+1) Bhutan (+975) Bolivia (+591) Bosnia & Herzegovina (+387) Botswana (+267) Brazil (+55) British Indian Ocean Territory (+246) British Virgin Islands (+1) B