    "https://jobs.ucf.edu/jobs/devops-engineer-iv-orlando-florida-united-states": {
      "title": "DevOps Engineer IV",
      "description": "DevOps Engineer IV - Orlando, Florida, United States University of Central Florida Navigation Home Meet Our People Featured Jobs Resources Faculty Join Our Talent Network Search Jobs Kiosk mode DevOps Engineer IV Information Technology (A&P) Skip to section BENEFITS WHY UCF? ABOUT ORLANDO My Profile Ready to Apply? DevOps Engineer IV R114434 Main Campus, Orlando, Florida Staff Full time Closing at: Oct 23 2026 - 12:00am EDT EIS- Enterprise Infrastructure University Operations: The University Operations division at UCF is committed to creating a supportive and welcoming environment for our faculty, staff, students, and the broader community. We take pride in delivering exceptional service, sharing our expertise, and upholding the highest standards to ensure a world-class campus experience. Visit our website or follow us on Facebook and Instagram to learn more. The Opportunity: The UCF IT division within University Operations is seeking a highly skilled DevOps Engineer IV to serve as the DevOps and Linux Platform Engineering Lead within UCF IT. This senior technical role is responsible for advancing cloud and Linux platform engineering practices across AWS, Google Cloud Platform (GCP), and enterprise Linux environments. The position will lead the design, implementation, automation, security, and operational excellence of cloud infrastructure and platform services that support the university's academic, research, and administrative missions. Classification Title: Cloud Computing Engineer IV Responsibilities: Lead the design, implementation, automation, and support of AWS cloud infrastructure and platform services supporting enterprise, academic, and research workloads. Develop and maintain Infrastructure as Code (IaC), CI/CD pipelines, cloud governance controls, monitoring solutions, backup and recovery processes, and operational standards. Engineer and support enterprise Linux platforms across cloud and on-premises environments, including configuration management, patching, automation, troubleshooting, and life cycle management. Design reusable automation solutions, scripts, templates, system images, and operational run-books to improve platform consistency and efficiency. Provide technical leadership for the university's Google Cloud Platform (GCP) environment, including cloud architecture, identity and access management, networking standards, monitoring, and automation. Develop and maintain DevOps, orchestration, and release engineering capabilities across cloud and Linux environments. Design, build, secure, and support containerized application platforms using Docker, including Docker image creation, multi-stage Docker builds, container registries, Docker Compose deployments, container networking, and operational best practices. Implement and maintain automated container build and deployment pipelines, integrating Docker technologies into CI/CD workflows to streamline application delivery and environment consistency. Implement automated deployment pipelines, testing frameworks, security controls, secrets management, and rollback procedures to improve service reliability and resilience. Establish cloud and platform engineering standards, architecture documentation, implementation guides, and operational procedures. Consult with university departments, researchers, developers, and technical teams regarding cloud adoption, application hosting, containerization strategies, automation opportunities, and modernization initiatives. Mentor technical staff in DevOps practices, cloud engineering, Linux administration, Docker technologies, automation, troubleshooting, and operational best practices. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 4 years of relevant experience; or High School Diploma (or equivalent) and 8 years of relevant work experience in lieu of degree; or an equivalent combination of education and experience pursuant to Fla. Stat. 112.219(6) . Preferred Qualifications : Experience supporting cloud infrastructure, DevOps practices, Linux platform administration, developing automation solutions, and supporting enterprise technology environments or systems engineering. Knowledge of cloud computing concepts, infrastructure management, security principles, and operational best practices. Strong analytical, problem-solving, and technical troubleshooting skills, with the ability to communicate effectively and collaborate with technical and non-technical stakeholders. Experience designing, implementing, and administering cloud environments within AWS and/or Google Cloud Platform (GCP). Experience developing and maintaining Infrastructure as Code (IaC) using tools such as Terraform, CloudFormation, or similar technologies. Experience building and supporting CI/CD pipelines, DevOps workflows, release engineering processes, and automated deployment solutions. Strong Linux systems administration experience, including configuration management, patching, automation, scripting, and performance tuning. Experience with scripting and automation languages such as Python, Bash, or PowerShell; containerization technologies including Docker; building container images with Docker Build; and deploying and managing multi-container applications using Docker Compose and modern application hosting technologies. Knowledge of cloud security, identity and access management, monitoring, observability, backup and recovery, and disaster recovery practices. Experience supporting large-scale enterprise, higher education, or research computing environments. Relevant certifications such as AWS Certified Solutions Architect, AWS Certified DevOps Engineer, Google Professional Cloud Architect, Red Hat certifications, Kubernetes certifications, Docker certifications, or equivalent credentials. Special Instructions to the Applicants: The anticipated salary range for this position is $108,150 to $115,000. The final salary will be determined based on the candidate's qualifications, experience, and internal equity considerations. If you are selected as the final candidate for an employment opportunity, both your position and salary will be significantly based upon the information that you have provided in your application for employment. We urge you to please take the time to complete the application in its entirety. All applicants must be authorized to work for any U.S. employer. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position, and the university cannot accommodate H‑1B transfers or employment-based visa processing for individuals currently sponsored by another employer. This role requires the successful candidate to work on-site at UCF as their primary work location. On-site presence is an essential function of this role. Classification Title: Cloud Computing Engineer IV Are you ready to unleash YOUR potential? As a next-generation public research university and Forbes-ranked top employer in Florida, we are a community of thinkers, doers, creators, innovators, healers, and leaders striving to create broader prosperity and help shape a better future. No matter what your role is, when you join Knight Nation, you’ll play an integral role at one of the most impactful universities in the country. You’ll be met with opportunities to connect and collaborate with talented faculty, staff, and students across 12 colleges and multiple campuses, engaging in impactful work that makes a positive difference. Your time at UCF will provide you with many meaningful opportunities to grow, you’ll work alongside talented colleagues on complex projects that will challenge you and help you gain new skills, and you’ll have countless rewarding experiences that go well beyond a paycheck. Working at UCF has its perks! UCF offers: Benefit packages, including Medical, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending, and Employee Assistance Program Paid time off, including annual and sick time off and paid holidays Retirement savings options Employee discounts, including tickets to many Orlando attractions Education assistance And more…For more benefits information, view the UCF Employee Benefits Guide . Dive into our Total Rewards Calculator to discover the diverse selection available to you, giving you a glimpse into the benefits that together shape your comprehensive rewards package at UCF. Unless explicitly stated on the job posting, it is UCF’s expectation that an employee of UCF will reside in Florida as of the date the employment begins. Department UCF IT Work Schedule Monday - Friday 8:00 AM - 5:00 PM Type of Appointment Regular Expected Salary $108,150.00 to Negotiable Job Posting End Date 10-23-2026-12-00-AM The University of Central Florida is an equal opportunity employer that does not discriminate against any employee or applicant for employment based on any characteristic protected by law.  The University maintains programs for protected veterans and individuals with disabilities in accordance with all applicable federal and state laws. As a Florida public university, the University of Central Florida makes all application materials and selection procedures available to the public upon request. UCF is proud to be a smoke-free campus and an E-Verify employer. For general application or posting questions, please email talent@ucf.edu . If an accommodation due to a disability is needed to apply for this position, please email onac@ucf.edu . People Also Viewed Plumber I Orlando Facilities (USPS) Data Engineer IV, Data Platforms Orlando Information Technology (A&P) Constituent Services Coordinator Orlando Administrative Management and (A&P) Want to be notified when we post new jobs?  Sign up here! First Name (required) 29b37ca7 Last Name (required) 53e1010b Email (required) 7c5c3142 Phone Number 32af131d 244 results found No results found Afghanistan (+93) Åland Islands (+358) Albania (+355) Algeria (+213) American Samoa (+1) Andorra (+376) Angola (+244) Anguilla (+1) Antigua & Barbuda (+1) Argentina (+54) Armenia (+374) Aruba (+297) As